{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790334710,"nonce":"Z30prCw8Vt6b1vEwG1XWf2RsYfI=","title":"An object literal nested in an array literal inside a typedef literal is built untyped","message":"`var tp:TypeParamDecl = {name: \"T\", meta: [{name: \":m\", params: [], pos: null}]}`: the inner literal gets no expected type (Metadata is a typedef of Array registered as a class when TypeParamDecl was typed), so its fields are stored as Dynamic values; `tp.meta[0].name` then reads an empty string. The same literal assigned from a local declared Array\u003cMetadataEntry\u003e reads correctly. Needs the expected type of an object literal field to see through such aliases when it propagates into an array literal's elements.","files":null}]}